# Certificates used ONLY as a fallback when a system cannot verify https://balanca.mdic.gov.br
# (R/balanca_tls.R). That server sends its leaf certificate but not the intermediate CA that
# issued it, and OpenSSL-based systems (Linux) do not fetch missing intermediates themselves.
# Both are public CA certificates. The pair is only ever given to libcurl as the trust anchors for
# requests to that one host, after the system's own trust store has failed -- see R/balanca_tls.R.
# Fetched 2026-10-21 from the AIA 'CA Issuers' URLs of the live certificates.
#
# [1] GlobalSign Root R46 -- self-signed root; also in Mozilla's CA store (checked)
#     valid from Mar 20 00:00:00 2019 GMT to Mar 20 00:00:00 2046 GMT 
#     SHA-256 4F:A3:12:6D:8D:3A:11:D1:C4:85:5A:4F:80:7C:BA:D6:CF:91:9D:3A:5A:88:B0:3B:EA:2C:63:72:D9:3C:40:C9
#     source: http://secure.globalsign.com/cacert/rootr46.crt
# [2] AC SERPRO AR46 OV TLS CA 2025 -- issued by [1]; CA:TRUE, pathlen:0, serverAuth only
#     valid from Oct 15 03:10:25 2025 GMT to Oct 15 00:00:00 2030 GMT 
#     SHA-256 F2:70:95:D0:B4:0D:F7:65:59:94:04:01:1C:F8:B1:67:DA:06:26:0E:81:DD:A7:27:F1:63:EF:08:22:10:71:E4
#     source: http://secure.globalsign.com/cacert/acserproar46ovtlsca2025.crt
#
# If SERPRO rotates the intermediate, replace [2] (the CI action .github/actions/trust-serpro-
# intermediate warns when the live one no longer matches); tests/testthat/test-balanca-tls.R
# fails before [2] expires.
